From: OpenX6X00 <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hashtable_init: clear the whole table, not a pointer's size of each entry

The memset took sizeof(callsign_hashtable), the pointer, where the malloc took the entry's size, so only the
first part of a new table was zeroed. A table freed and allocated again (the FT8 app closed and opened) could
then show calls from before as if they had just been heard.
---
 ft8/hashtable.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/ft8/hashtable.c
+++ b/ft8/hashtable.c
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
     callsign_hashtable_size = 0;
     callsign_hashtable_max_size = hashtable_max_size;
     callsign_hashtable = malloc(sizeof(*callsign_hashtable) * callsign_hashtable_max_size);
-    memset(callsign_hashtable, 0, sizeof(callsign_hashtable) * callsign_hashtable_max_size);
+    memset(callsign_hashtable, 0, sizeof(*callsign_hashtable) * callsign_hashtable_max_size);
 }
 
 void hashtable_delete()
